1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,863
The Sikh Police Who Came in 1881,

2
00:00:02,943 --> 00:00:05,975
and the Community They Left Behind

3
00:00:05,975 --> 00:00:11,112
On the 26th of March 1881 an
assistant superintendent and 54 Sikh

4
00:00:11,192 --> 00:00:16,248
recruits from Punjab arrived in
Singapore to join a police force

5
00:00:16,328 --> 00:00:21,625
that was struggling to keep order
in a crowded, fast-growing port.

6
00:00:21,625 --> 00:00:24,481
By the end of the year the Sikh

7
00:00:24,561 --> 00:00:27,875
Police Contingent numbered 165 men.

8
00:00:27,875 --> 00:00:30,661
The contingent was disbanded in 1945,

9
00:00:30,741 --> 00:00:34,843
but the community that grew
up around it, with its own

10
00:00:34,923 --> 00:00:38,950
gurdwara on Silat Road, is
still in Singapore today.

11
00:00:38,950 --> 00:00:44,025
The first Sikhs recorded in
Singapore did not come as policemen.

12
00:00:44,025 --> 00:00:46,733
In 1850 two Sikh political prisoners,

13
00:00:46,813 --> 00:00:50,727
Bhai Maharaj Singh and
Khurruck Singh, were exiled to

14
00:00:50,807 --> 00:00:54,650
Singapore by the British
after they annexed Punjab.

15
00:00:54,650 --> 00:00:57,952
The police recruitment
came three decades later,

16
00:00:58,032 --> 00:01:00,075
and it had a practical cause.

17
00:01:00,075 --> 00:01:04,019
In the 1870s the Straits
Settlements Police faced high

18
00:01:04,099 --> 00:01:08,192
crime and the influence of
the Chinese secret societies,

19
00:01:08,272 --> 00:01:11,775
and the force had long
had trouble keeping men.

20
00:01:11,775 --> 00:01:16,368
A police report in 1856 had
already complained that officers

21
00:01:16,448 --> 00:01:20,730
could not understand Chinese
speakers, that pay was low,

22
00:01:20,810 --> 00:01:25,950
and that many Indian policemen
went home after two or three years.

23
00:01:25,950 --> 00:01:30,250
In 1879 a commission of
enquiry into the police

24
00:01:30,330 --> 00:01:34,150
recommended recruiting Sikhs from Punjab.

25
00:01:34,150 --> 00:01:37,664
According to the Singapore
Police Force's own history,

26
00:01:37,744 --> 00:01:41,658
the colonial government chose
them because of the reputation

27
00:01:41,738 --> 00:01:45,718
Sikh soldiers had in British
service, and because Sikh police

28
00:01:45,798 --> 00:01:49,525
had already been used in Hong
Kong and the Malay States.

29
00:01:49,525 --> 00:01:53,902
The first group landed on
the 26th of March 1881,

30
00:01:53,982 --> 00:01:58,075
the day after a batch
of European constables.

31
00:01:58,075 --> 00:02:02,902
About 100 Sikh policemen
were in Singapore by August,

32
00:02:02,982 --> 00:02:08,075
and a full contingent of 165
had assembled by November.

33
00:02:08,075 --> 00:02:11,450
The European constables
did not adapt well to

34
00:02:11,530 --> 00:02:14,829
local conditions and
were disbanded by 1906,

35
00:02:14,909 --> 00:02:18,825
while the Sikhs became a
lasting part of the force.

36
00:02:18,825 --> 00:02:21,625
The terms of service were strict.

37
00:02:21,625 --> 00:02:25,950
Recruits had to be at least
175 centimetres tall with

38
00:02:26,030 --> 00:02:30,273
a chest of more than 96.5
centimetres, and they were

39
00:02:30,353 --> 00:02:34,675
medically examined and sworn
in before a magistrate.

40
00:02:34,675 --> 00:02:38,708
They were also baptised at the
contingent's own gurdwara and

41
00:02:38,788 --> 00:02:42,340
had to follow the code of
conduct for baptised Sikhs,

42
00:02:42,420 --> 00:02:47,150
which meant keeping their hair and
beards uncut and wearing a turban.

43
00:02:47,150 --> 00:02:52,075
The contingent kept order in town
and guarded government buildings.

44
00:02:52,075 --> 00:02:56,503
A riot squad of 50 men was
kept on standby at all times,

45
00:02:56,583 --> 00:02:59,562
and Sikh officers accompanied visiting

46
00:02:59,642 --> 00:03:03,425
dignitaries and took part
in ceremonial duties.

47
00:03:03,425 --> 00:03:07,375
Later they also took on
beat and traffic duties.

48
00:03:07,375 --> 00:03:13,084
A detachment was sent to Christmas Island,
then part of the Straits Settlements,

49
00:03:13,164 --> 00:03:17,000
where it dealt with labour
unrest in the early 1900s.

50
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,730
The contingent's reputation made Sikh

51
00:03:19,810 --> 00:03:23,075
guards the choice of
private employers too.

52
00:03:23,075 --> 00:03:28,225
The Tanjong Pagar Dock Company
hired Sikhs as its dock police.

53
00:03:28,225 --> 00:03:32,213
Others guarded the Straits
Trading Company's tin smelter

54
00:03:32,293 --> 00:03:37,226
on Pulau Brani, the Shell Company's
oil storage tanks on Pulau Sambu,

55
00:03:37,306 --> 00:03:40,575
and the granite quarries
at Bukit Timah Hill.

56
00:03:40,575 --> 00:03:43,890
The contingent built
its own gurdwara at its

57
00:03:43,970 --> 00:03:47,285
barracks in 1882, the
year after it arrived,

58
00:03:47,365 --> 00:03:51,300
and it served civilian
Sikhs as well as the police.

59
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:53,526
As more Sikhs came to Singapore,

60
00:03:53,606 --> 00:03:56,200
the community grew beyond the force.

61
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:59,770
In 1912 civilian Sikhs,
in a committee led by the

62
00:03:59,850 --> 00:04:02,526
merchant Wassiamull Assomull Mahtani,

63
00:04:02,606 --> 00:04:07,225
bought a compound on Queen Street
for a gurdwara of their own.

64
00:04:07,225 --> 00:04:12,015
The police Sikhs then petitioned
for land of their own, and in 1922

65
00:04:12,095 --> 00:04:16,958
they obtained a site on Silat Road
from the Singapore Harbour Board,

66
00:04:17,038 --> 00:04:21,400
the body that had taken over
the Tanjong Pagar Dock Company.

67
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:25,602
The Straits Times of the 19th
of December 1922 reported that

68
00:04:25,682 --> 00:04:30,027
the foundation stone had been
laid the previous morning by the

69
00:04:30,107 --> 00:04:33,881
Inspector-General of Police,
Captain A. R. Chancellor,

70
00:04:33,961 --> 00:04:39,100
"in the presence of practically the
entire Sikh community in Singapore."

71
00:04:39,100 --> 00:04:43,208
The address read to him that day
explained that Singapore's Sikhs

72
00:04:43,288 --> 00:04:48,104
had long needed a place of worship and
a lodging house close to the wharves,

73
00:04:48,184 --> 00:04:52,050
for the members of their community
passing through the port.

74
00:04:52,050 --> 00:04:56,294
The paper reported that $22,000
had already been raised,

75
00:04:56,374 --> 00:05:00,155
with contributions from
Sikhs across the peninsula

76
00:05:00,235 --> 00:05:04,250
and from Sikh police in
other parts of the Far East.

77
00:05:04,250 --> 00:05:07,457
That evening the Sikhs
held a farewell reception

78
00:05:07,537 --> 00:05:10,550
for Chancellor at the
Pearl's Hill barracks.

79
00:05:10,550 --> 00:05:15,822
The gurdwara was completed
in 1924 at a cost of $54,000,

80
00:05:15,902 --> 00:05:21,350
most of it raised by Sikh
police in Singapore and Malaya.

81
00:05:21,350 --> 00:05:24,783
It was the first gurdwara
in Singapore built in

82
00:05:24,863 --> 00:05:28,600
the traditional Sikh style,
with domes and arches.

83
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:32,566
During the Japanese occupation
it housed and looked after

84
00:05:32,646 --> 00:05:36,541
the widows and children of
Sikhs, and after the war many

85
00:05:36,621 --> 00:05:40,525
of the widows were offered
free passage home to Punjab.

86
00:05:40,525 --> 00:05:44,625
The Sikh Police Contingent
did not survive the war.

87
00:05:44,625 --> 00:05:48,864
The National Library Board's
history of the police attributes

88
00:05:48,944 --> 00:05:52,829
its disbandment in 1945 to a
high attrition rate and low

89
00:05:52,909 --> 00:05:57,148
morale after the Japanese
occupation, during which some Sikhs

90
00:05:57,228 --> 00:06:01,326
had faced what it calls divided
loyalties, and to shrinking

91
00:06:01,406 --> 00:06:05,300
recruitment once India and
Pakistan became independent.

92
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:08,008
Individual Sikh officers continued

93
00:06:08,088 --> 00:06:10,875
to serve in the police afterwards.

94
00:06:10,875 --> 00:06:16,043
In 1949 the police formed a new
guard force recruited from Nepal,

95
00:06:16,123 --> 00:06:20,725
the Gurkha Contingent, to take
over the Sikh unit's role.

96
00:06:20,725 --> 00:06:24,250
The community outlasted the contingent.

97
00:06:24,250 --> 00:06:28,256
Singapore had 12,051
resident Sikhs in 2020,

98
00:06:28,336 --> 00:06:33,456
and the Silat Road gurdwara,
rebuilt behind its original

99
00:06:33,536 --> 00:06:37,449
façade and reopened in
1995, was declared a

100
00:06:37,529 --> 00:06:42,450
historic site by the National
Heritage Board in 1999.

101
00:06:42,450 --> 00:06:46,586
Where it fits in the bigger
story: Singapore's police history

102
00:06:46,666 --> 00:06:50,675
is usually told through its
commissioners and its reforms.

103
00:06:50,675 --> 00:06:55,493
The Sikh Police Contingent was
recruited to solve a specific problem,

104
00:06:55,573 --> 00:06:59,893
a force that could not keep men
or be trusted to stay clear of

105
00:06:59,973 --> 00:07:04,800
the secret societies, and it did
that job for more than sixty years.

106
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:07,813
The men it brought from
Punjab, and the guards and

107
00:07:07,893 --> 00:07:11,091
families who followed them,
built a gurdwara near the

108
00:07:11,171 --> 00:07:15,112
wharves with their own money, and
it is the community they built,

109
00:07:15,192 --> 00:07:17,975
rather than the police
unit, that has lasted.
